Description: Modifications to OpenWebRX for amateur radio stations
 ABMod adds to OpenWebRX a bookmarks panel inside the receiver, an editable
 band plan, real access control with user management, 5-tone (SELCALL) and
 2-tone paging decoders, a map drawn with Leaflet on OpenStreetMap instead of
 the Google Maps API, APRS in both directions, and an importer for a national
 repeater list that works out from the terrain which stations are actually
 receivable.
 .
 It is not a fork. It replaces 31 files of the openwebrx package, using dpkg
 diversions so the originals are kept beside them and restored when this
 package is removed, and adds 19 of its own. Your settings, bookmarks and users
 are never touched.
 .
 Because whole files are replaced, this package is tied to the exact OpenWebRX
 version it was built against. Installing it will hold openwebrx at that
 version; removing it lets openwebrx upgrade again.

